      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SALLY BIGTIME (5) put the writing on the wall with back-to-back placings before returning to the winners' list here last week, leading to score by 2m. Draws a couple of spots wider but is proven at this longer distance so could go on with it. Manners let GOLDEN FIRE NZ (7) down last week but she was going well prior with a placing two back and three straight wins prior. She came from this barrier in two of those so is good enough with her A-game. ISLA ROCHELLE (2) had been racing consistently before coming from a wider barrier for a last-start win by 1.5 metres at this circuit and distance. The low draw could see her strike again. LUVARESCHS (6) can be competitive again having continued her solid form with a placing last week.",
